# What this file does here: `require_code_owner_reviews` is OFF on main, so
# these entries do NOT gate a merge. They only make GitHub auto-request the
# right reviewers when a PR touches a path. Main needs 1 approval, and any
# teammate with write access can give it — so whoever is tagged can unblock a
# PR without waiting for the repo owner.
#
# Note you cannot approve your own PR. That is why the default line lists
# everyone: whoever opens a PR, the other three still get asked.
#
# Lanes below follow who has actually been working where (see docs/TEAM.md).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

